  "subtitle": "Research at Slop University",
  "summary": "A short film from Slop University sets out the conviction its research begins from: that what the University measures, it comes to understand, and what it understands, it can improve. Three recent studies, of a staff-kitchen urn of ginger tea, a river sampled from a bridge and the fryer oil of four club canteens, show that conviction at work in each of the University's schools. The film closes on the University's research performance since July, from its output per academic to its citations and its funding.",
